      "message": "Aaron, we\u0027ll talk in the morning, but I think you can use this to start. I believe that bb_retimer, bma255, tcpci_generic, and ps8xxx should be working with this (or at least close to working). As you can see it required re-architecting how the emul_common_i2c worked. Basically, we need to relinquish control over the i2c_emul struct, but in the case of the ps8xxx we do need to create an additional 3 instances and register them. We then run a series of if...else if on the address to figure out which sub-chip we\u0027re talking to.\n\nWe\u0027ll sync in the morning.",
